Build a failure explanation from preserved history, competing mechanisms, and independent tests (@metal-failure-analysis: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC", #source "../sources/ASM-Mechanical-Testing-and-Evaluation.lingua#r_1VW327STC5YQGRAPNRAPQSZQNG", #source "../sources/ASM-Metallography-and-Microstructures.lingua#r_4XHEJ1ZHW0B1YNG9AWCEC491ME", #source "../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "../../../engineering/mining-and-mineral-engineering/processing/Metallurgical-accounting-reconciliation-and-grade-control.lingua#r_1CS10W97ZP2WS11B5PZHAEGFP1") { r_2BKHB12DXF3EBH7VH8M2H22YGX
**Read:** [Mechanical Behavior of Materials — Krystyn Van Vliet, MIT 3.22](../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC), the complete failure/mechanism and special-topic study; [Mechanical Testing and Evaluation — ASM Handbook, volume 8](../sources/ASM-Mechanical-Testing-and-Evaluation.lingua#r_1VW327STC5YQGRAPNRAPQSZQNG), all complete relevant test/evaluation chapters, when available; [Metallography and Microstructures — ASM Handbook, volume 9](../sources/ASM-Metallography-and-Microstructures.lingua#r_4XHEJ1ZHW0B1YNG9AWCEC491ME), whole relevant preparation, structure/fracture interpretation, and alloy chapters, when available; [Metals, alloys, steels, and graduate modeling — Bhadeshia teaching materials](../sources/Metals-Alloys-and-Graduate-Teaching-Bhadeshia.lingua#r_0HZJKN8WC6SEWA0DABM8P4HC3F), full applicable fracture, embrittlement, weld, and service-material discussions.

Begin with what happened, the material/component function, load/environment history, observed sequence, and preserved evidence. Separate initiating conditions, damage mechanisms, final separation, and consequential changes after the event. A striking fracture image or a familiar defect is not by itself a complete causal account.

Connect design/specification, material identity, fabrication/heat/joining history, service, inspection, maintenance, and relevant changes. Choose nondestructive, dimensional, chemical, metallographic, fractographic, and mechanical methods for the hypotheses, preserving what each preparation or test changes. Unavailable history is a limitation to investigate, not a licence to invent it.

Compare genuinely competing explanations and identify evidence each would predict. A mechanism-consistent observation may still be compatible with another cause. Distinguish a local defect, a process/system cause, and a proposed corrective action; the latter needs its own test of consequences and recurrence.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public failure investigation with full primary methods and material/service evidence. Independently reproduce a significant structural, chemical, or mechanics calculation and challenge the preferred cause with an alternative. Design a discriminating test or observation and evaluate the proposed correction against actual function and variability. Explain the residual uncertainty and how the production/inspection/maintenance record would preserve what another team needs to learn from the case.

**Continue:** [Reconcile production accounts without concealing uncertainty or changing the question](../../../engineering/mining-and-mineral-engineering/processing/Metallurgical-accounting-reconciliation-and-grade-control.lingua#r_1CS10W97ZP2WS11B5PZHAEGFP1).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
